BT 1 0 0 1 0 254.7 Tm 13.2 TL /F1 9.3 Tf .105882 .152941 .2 rg (Three themes dominated this window. First, ) Tj /F2 9.3 Tf (unpatched or barely-patched pre-auth flaws in internet-facing) Tj T* (software) Tj /F1 9.3 Tf (, several exploited before disclosure: Sansec's ) Tj /F2 9.3 Tf (StyleSmuggler) Tj /F1 9.3 Tf ( Magento/Adobe Commerce zero-day \(now) Tj T* (CVE-2026-75650, CVSS 10.0, attacks from 4 Sep, hotfix only on 7 Sep\), CERT Polska's ) Tj /F2 9.3 Tf (MikroTrick) Tj /F1 9.3 Tf ( RouterOS SSH) Tj T* -0.034767 Tw (takeover \(exploited from 2 Sep, three days ahead of disclosure\), Sangoma Switchvox and JFrog Artifactory both landing) Tj T* 0 Tw (on CISA KEV, and ~22,000 Exchange servers still exposed to CVE-2026-62911 with public exploit code. Second, ) Tj /F2 9.3 Tf (the) Tj T* (software supply chain was attacked at three different layers in one week) Tj /F1 9.3 Tf ( - the network route \(a BGP hijack served) Tj T* (a malicious Virtualizor update that took root on hosting hypervisors\), the registry endpoint \(Coder's Cloudflare pool was) Tj T* (repointed to serve credential-stealing Terraform modules for 14 hours\), and the vendor's own CI \(JetBrains was) Tj T* (breached through an unpatched TeamCity, the product it ships, and told Cadence users to rotate everything\). Signature) Tj T* (and provenance checks did not help in any of the three, because in each case the thing trusted was not the artefact.) Tj T* (Third, ) Tj /F2 9.3 Tf (AI moved from research finding to operational fact) Tj /F1 9.3 Tf (: Unit 42 worked a real incident where autonomous agents) Tj T* (breached an enterprise in under 10 hours using no zero-day, Forescout used Claude to port a pre-auth PLC exploit to a) Tj T* (new hardware model for $536, Manifold's ) Tj /F2 9.3 Tf (GitSpawn) Tj /F1 9.3 Tf ( flaws let untrusted repositories run commands outside seven) Tj T* (coding agents' sandboxes, and UAC-0099 planted a nuclear-weapon prompt in a VBS comment purely to make LLM) Tj T* (analysis abort. Regionally, no new Australian incident was logged but two ACSC alerts remain open and directly) Tj T* (relevant \(the CMS webshell campaign and in-country N-able N-central exploitation\); APAC saw a DPRK-linked) Tj T* (backdoor compiled into victims' own HAProxy binaries in South Korea and malicious Packagist themes turning) Tj T* (Vietnamese streaming sites into an iOS spyware delivery surface. Identity data took the heaviest breach hit: 153M) Tj T* (driver's licence scans traced to IDScan.net, 9.5M patients at Aesto Health, and sealed court filings from Thomson) Tj T* (Reuters' C-Track.) Tj T* ET
